From: Kunstbanause <3209654+Kunstbanause@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:24:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] d/rift_s: Add IMU + optical error-state Kalman filter for
 controllers

Strapdown ESKF (orientation, position, velocity, gyro and accel bias)
driven by the controller IMU and corrected by delayed constellation
poses. States are kept for 400 ms so optical fixes are applied at their
exposure time and the IMU is replayed, and so that past-time queries
give the constellation tracker accurate priors. Outliers are gated by
Mahalanobis distance, short occlusions are bridged by dead reckoning
with velocity decay, longer ones hold the position.

Design and starting values follow the OpenHMD Rift CV1 6DoF UKF.
Not wired into the driver yet; covered by synthetic-trajectory tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
